            "paragraph": "The observed meteorological data were extracted from SPAIN02 (Herrera et al. 2012), a monthly climate dataset of observed precipitation and temperature from 1950 to 2015. SPAIN02 is a high-resolution daily and monthly gridded precipitation and temperature data- set with a resolution of 0.2\u00b0 over the Iberian Peninsula. It was developed from the main gauging stations of the Spanish Meteorological Agency (Agencia Estatal de Meteorolog\u00eda, AEMET) using kriging algorithms. The hydrological data were extracted from the PATRI- CAL model, which contains monthly streamflow series re-natured from historical gauged series in Spain (Mu\u00f1oz 2016).",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "T\u00e9mez hydrological model",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "HAS_METRIC",
            "target_entity_instance": "Kling-Gupta Efficiency (KGE)",
            "target_entity_type": "Metric",
            "paragraph": "The T\u00e9mez hydrological model is a lumped, conceptual rainfall\u2013runoff model dividing a basin into an unsaturated soil (upper) zone and a saturated aquifer (lower) storage, used at a monthly scale for water-balance and streamflow simulation (P\u00e9rez-S\u00e1nchez et al. 2019). For the Turia River basin case, the model was discretised in 5 sub-basins delimited by streamflow gauges and existing reservoirs (Fig. 1). Its parameters were calibrated for the 1961-1990 period against the streamflow dataset of the PATRICAL model. The Kling- Gupta Efficiency (KGE) and its components were used as an objective function for manual and automatic calibration methods.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "RCP4.5",
            "source_entity_type": "Experiment",
            "relation": "PART_OF_PROJECT",
            "target_entity_instance": "EURO-CORDEX",
            "target_entity_type": "Project",
            "paragraph": "Monthly precipitation, temperature, and in-month maximum and minimum temperatures were acquired for 18 climate models (See the Detailed list in the Supplementary Mate- rial) from the EURO-CORDEX initiative (Earth System Grid Federation 2021; Jacob et al. 2014). The 18 combinations correspond to all EURO-CORDEX RCP4.5 and RCP8.5 runs at the EUR-44 resolution that consistently provide the complete set of required variables (pr, tas, tasmax, tasmin); although the present analysis focuses on RCP8.5, this pre-selec- tion ensured dataset consistency across scenarios. The preselected models include combina- tions of 10 General Circulation Models (GCMs) and 8 Regional Climate Models (RCMs). Although the methodology framework can be fully transferable and implemented regarding the climate change product employed, the Representative Concentration Pathway (RCP) 8.5 emission scenario was chosen for analysis. Although certain simulations within EURO- CORDEX have been subject to documented limitations (e.g., IPSL-CM5A_INERIS-WRF; Kotlarski et al. 2014), all available members meeting the variable requirements were used to preserve the integrity of the ensemble decision space.",
